  "line": 240,
  "title": "Create the member identity atomically and return the stored winner",
  "detail": "`memberId` reads `member.id`, then writes a new value unconditionally (~243). Two processes opening the same database for the first time can both read nothing. B stores and returns its ID, then A overwrites it with another, so B's identity changes after a restart. That breaks \"created once\" and the stable owner identity claims depend on.\nReproduced with a deterministic interleaving through two SQLite connections (two different IDs returned).\nInsert only when absent (one statement, for example `INSERT OR IGNORE`, or a transaction), then read the stored value back and return that. Keep the deterministic two-connection test, asserting both callers return the same stored ID."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/integrations/claim-ref.ts",
  "line": 100,
  "title": "Share the repository-tree load between concurrent callers with different abort signals",
  "detail": "The cache starts another `load()` whenever the pending entry was started with a different abort signal (~100). Two writes to different refs that share one client and repository but use separate signals therefore send two tree POSTs. Numbered test 8 requires one per repository per instance.\nReproduced: a test expecting one tree request received two.\nStart one shared load per key, and let each caller wait for it under its own signal, so that one caller's abort rejects only that caller. If the shared load fails, drop the entry so the next caller retries.\nTests: two concurrent callers with different signals make one request. Aborting one caller still lets the other succeed."
 },
